process=[
('1','Before transfer','Counsel checks trust funding, title, beneficiaries, relationship, powers, debts, prior gifts and estate inclusion. Separate the Inheritor’s own assets from the Transferor’s estate.','Planning action; trust alone is not tax exemption.','estate'),
('2','At death / immediately','Trustee secures property and documents; contact insurer about occupancy, vacancy and landlord coverage. Preserve records privately.','Practical safeguard, not a quoted statutory deadline.','insurance'),
('3','Trust notification','Determine who must receive statutory notice. Generally serve within 60 days of triggering event, with statutory awareness/vacancy exceptions.','Counsel confirms deadline and service.','trust'),
('4','Inventory and appraisal','Record date-of-death values, liabilities, gifts and potential deductions. Obtain defensible appraisal and review basis consistency.','Alternative valuation requires specific eligibility/election.','basis'),
('5','Assessor reporting','File applicable death/change-in-ownership reports; confirm trust-transfer date, supplemental assessments and deadlines with assessor.','Exact county forms/deadlines not verified here; do not rely on the one-year residence rule for all filings.','boe'),
('6','Within one year if seeking family-home relief','Establish genuine eligible principal residence and file homeowners’ (BOE-266) or disabled-veterans’ exemption BEFORE filing BOE-19-P.','Confirm transferor residence, relationship and continuing use; moving out later cancels exclusion next Jan 1 lien date (date-of-death FMV indexed).','boepub'),
('7','Exclusion claim','BOE Pub. 800-1 says file BOE-19-P within three years or before transfer to third party (or within 6 months of supplemental/escape notice); confirm any late/prospective relief rules.','Distinct from one-year exemption deadline; BOE-266 must be filed first.','boepub'),
('8','Generally nine months after death','Executor reviews Form 706 filing requirement, portability and payment; six-month filing extension may be available.','An extension to file is not automatic permission to delay tax payment.','faq'),
('9','Before distribution / implementation','Reserve for tax and debts; compare real sale offers against verified rental and occupancy budgets. Document beneficiary authority and decision.','Do not distribute liquidity needed for settlement.','estate'),
('10','After implementation / annually','Update coverage, rent compliance, accounting, assessment and portfolio allocation; re-run after legal or economic changes.','Current facts must replace old scenarios.','sec')]
TIMELINE=[
('Day 0 · date of death','Reference date for inherited basis and for the property-tax clocks. Counsel fixes the effective transfer date; the date of distribution or recording can differ.','Date-of-death value is generally the starting basis; trust alone does not guarantee an adjustment.','basis'),
('Within 9 months after death · tax also due','Federal estate-tax return (Form 706) if a filing requirement exists. The tax itself is due in the same 9 months. Form 4768 gives an automatic 6-month extension to file and can separately request an extension of time to pay; an extension to file does not by itself extend payment.','In one IRS document (Form 706 instructions, Rev. July 2026): “You must file Form 706 ... within 9 months after the date of the decedent’s death” and “The estate and GST taxes are due within 9 months of the date of the decedent’s death.” Filing is required only above the year-of-death threshold ($15,000,000 for 2026 deaths).',['irc6075','estate']),
 ('Up to 5 years after death · only if no filing requirement existed','A late portability election may still be possible: an executor with no filing requirement who did not file on time may file Form 706 on or before the fifth anniversary of the death under the procedure the instructions name.','Form 706 instructions: executors eligible under Rev. Proc. 2022-32 may file on or before the fifth anniversary of the decedent’s death, and must state on the return that it is filed under that procedure. A timely return is still required for the ordinary portability election.','irc6075'),
 ('60 days after the triggering event','Trustee serves the statutory notification on beneficiaries and heirs, and on the Attorney General for a charitable trust. The period runs from the event, or from when the trustee learns of a person entitled to notice, and from the date a new trustee begins to serve if there was a vacancy.','Probate Code §16061.7(f): service “not later than 60 days following the occurrence of the event requiring service”. Counsel confirms who must be served and the method.','trust'),
('Within 1 year of transfer','Homeowners’ exemption claim (BOE-266) if family-home relief is sought. Must be filed before the exclusion claim.','BOE Prop 19 page: file for the homeowners’ exemption within 1 year of transfer.','boe'),
('Within 3 years, or before a third-party transfer','Claim for exclusion (BOE-19-P) from reassessment, with the eligibility facts documented.','BOE Prop 19 page: claim for exclusion within 3 years or before transfer to a third party.','boe'),
('Each year · sale year and later','California Form 540 return and payment. For 2025 returns the booklet lists April 15, 2026 to file and pay, and October 15, 2026 for the extended filing date. Check the year’s booklet each time.','The 1% Behavioral Health Services Tax on taxable income above $1,000,000 is reported on Line 62.','ftb540'),
('Before any sale, listing or contract','If a like-kind route is considered at all: replacement real property must be identified on or before 45 days after the transfer, and received by the earlier of 180 days after the transfer or the due date (with extensions) of the return for the year of transfer. Since the 2017 law only real property qualifies, and the property given up must have been held for productive use in a trade or business or for investment.','irc1031'),
('At any new year-end','Recheck the federal exclusion, the filing threshold and any proposed legislation. The 2027 federal exclusion is published; later years are not.','Rules change; re-read the linked source on the decision date.','irs27')]

('Every 12 months · before the decision, then annually','Re-read the federal exclusion and annual gift exclusion, the SALT cap for the year, the Proposition 19 allowance in force, the county assessment and the actual bills; record the date and what changed beside each item.','The exclusion is published year by year (2026: $15,000,000; 2027: $15,480,000; annual gift exclusion $19,000 then $20,000); the Proposition 19 allowance is re-indexed and published in BOE notices; nothing here replaces the figures in force on the decision date.',['irs27','allow','boe']),page('process.html','From trust to decision','PRACTICAL ROADMAP / 05','Use Transferor, Trustee and Inheritor as placeholders. Keep personal documents out of a public repository.',table('General sequence · not a substitute for trust-specific legal administration',['Step','Timing','Action','Caution','Official context'],process)+table('Deadline timeline · counted from the date of death; each row is a rule read on its official page',['When','What is due','Rule as read','Official context'],TIMELINE)+notice('Separate clocks and separate taxes','Date of death, trust distribution and deed recording need not be the same date for tax purposes. Estate tax, capital-gains basis and property-tax reassessment are different systems. Have counsel establish the effective transfer date; do not delay eligibility work until distribution.'))

laws=[
('Federal estate tax · 2026','$15,000,000','Gross estate plus relevant adjusted taxable gifts determines filing; estate deductions/credits determine tax. U.S. citizen/resident rules; nonresident noncitizens differ.','estate'),
('Federal estate tax · 2027','$15,480,000','Published November 5, 2026; not an estimate and not a per-heir exemption.','irs27'),
('Estate scope','Cash, securities, real estate and potentially insurance/trust assets','Already-owned assets of the Inheritor are not automatically the Transferor’s assets; inspect actual interests. No private inventory published.','estate'),
('Portability','Timely Form 706 election generally needed','Do not automatically double the exclusion for a married couple.','faq'),
('California death taxes','No CA estate-tax return for deaths from January 1, 2005','Current Controller guidance; older inheritance-tax administration concerns deaths before June 8, 1982. Future law unknown.','sco'),
('Inherited basis','Generally date-of-death fair market value','Alternate valuation and exceptions apply; adjusted assessment for property tax is NOT the same as income-tax basis.','basis'),
('Trust exception','Some irrevocable grantor-trust property gets no §1014 adjustment','Revenue Ruling 2023-2 concerns assets outside deceased grantor gross estate. Never assume step-up merely because title is in trust.','trustbasis'),
('Prop 13 assessment','Annual factored-base increase capped at 2%','Taxable value generally lower of factored base and market; market recovery from temporary decline can exceed 2%. Reassessment/new construction are separate.','rtc'),
('Prop 19 allowance','$1,044,590 displayed to $10','Rounded public-law amount only. Official legal amount is available at linked notice; use the exact legal figure for filings. Applies February 16, 2025–February 15, 2027; future allowance unknown.','allow'),
('Qualifying family home','Old factored base + max(0, market − old base − applicable allowance)','Requires eligible relationship, transferor/transferee principal residence and claims. No general rental-home exclusion. Continued eligibility matters.','boe'),
('Local tax rate / direct charges','','Not published: city-specific rates and local rent rules are withheld from this public guide. Confirm the applicable tax area and coverage privately from current records.','rtc'),
('Home-sale gain exclusion','Up to $250,000 / $500,000 if qualified','Generally own/use two of five years; not automatic upon inheritance. Depreciation/nonqualified use may affect exclusion.','sell'),
('California capital gains','No lower rate; gains are taxed as ordinary income','Ordinary-income treatment confirmed on the FTB capital-gains page.','ftb'),
('Behavioral Health Services Tax (1% add-on)','1% of California taxable income above $1,000,000','Form 540 Line 62 (2025 instructions, read 2026-11-16): if taxable income is more than $1,000,000, compute 1% of the amount above $1,000,000. Imposed by RTC §17043 for taxable years beginning on or after January 1, 2005. The threshold is not adjusted in these instructions; a large one-year gain can reach it.',['ftb540','t117043']),
('Personal SALT itemized cap','$40,000 (2025) / $40,400 (2026); the statute sets 101% of the prior year for each year 2027–2029 and returns to $10,000 for years beginning after 2029 unless later law changes it','The 2026 amount is stated on the IRS correction page for the 2026 Form 1040-ES, which also gives the phase-down threshold ($505,000; $252,500 married filing separately) and the $10,000 floor. For 2027 the amount is arithmetic on the statute (101% of $40,400), not a figure read on an IRS page. This is the individual Schedule A itemized-deduction cap, not a property-specific rental-tax calculation; no personal deduction is assumed.',['saltcorr','saltlaw','sched_a']),
('Rental income','Taxable with qualifying expenses and depreciation','Mixed-use allocation, capital improvements, passive losses and possible NIIT matter. Gross rent is not profit.','rent'),
('Savings insurance','$250,000 per depositor / insured bank / ownership category','Aggregate deposits in same category; investments such as stocks and mutual funds are not FDIC insured.','fdic'),
('Law watch · SB 974','Chaptered September 27, 2026, Chapter 665','Enacted special-needs-trust transfer-medium amendment, not a pending blanket restoration of the old parent-child exclusion. Household relevance unknown; confirm effective application with counsel.','bill'),
('Nov 2026 California ballot (unofficial)','Nov 14 (5:16 p.m.): Prop 3 Yes 60.7%, Prop 40 No 52.2%, Prop 42 Yes 51.3%','No Prop 19 repeal appeared on the Nov 2026 ballot; unofficial until Dec 11 certification. Recheck federal legislation and BOE updates at decision time.','sos26'),
('Proposition H · city parcel tax for Muni (approved Nov 3, 2026)','Multifamily parcel: $249 a year up to 5,000 sq ft of building area, plus $0.195 per sq ft above 5,000 (maximum $50,000). Single-family: $129 up to 3,000 sq ft, plus $0.42 and $1.99 per sq ft above that. Runs July 1, 2027 to June 30, 2042.','Official SFMTA page (read 2026-11-16) says voters approved it on 2026-11-03; first bill is fiscal year 2027-28. Rates rise with inflation from fiscal year 2028-29. Renters: landlord pass-through up to 50%, capped at $65 per unit a year, not for base rent set on or after June 1, 2027. Building area and parcel type are private; check them with SFMTA and the Assessor.','sfmta26')]
