page('law.html','Tax & law','OFFICIAL RULES / 06','Current rules reviewed on the per-source dates shown below—not a promise of rules at a future inheritance.',notice('How to read this page','Every row is either a rule read on the linked official page in this session, or it says what is not verified. Displayed legal amounts are rounded to $10 where a fraction appears; the linked authority always governs. Rules can change before any transfer; re-read them at the time of action.')+table('Current rules · displayed legal dollars rounded to $10 where necessary; exact authority remains linked',['Topic','Verified rule / amount','Limits','Official source'],laws)+'''<h2>Proposition H schedule · official rates</h2><p>The complete published schedule for the city parcel tax, for FY 2027–28 bills. Official rates are shown exactly as published: they are public statutory amounts, not household figures, so the $10 display rule does not apply to them. Agency examples: a 2,000 sq ft single-family home pays $129; a 4,000 sq ft single-family home pays $549; a 20,000 sq ft apartment building pays $3,174. Amounts rise with inflation from FY 2028–29. The Controller estimates about $177 million a year. Applying the schedule to any parcel needs that parcel’s official building area, which is not published here.</p>'''+table('Proposition H parcel tax · annual tax, FY 2027–28, official schedule',['Parcel type','Building area','Annual tax (FY 2027–28)','Official source'],prop_h_rows)+'''<h2>How much room remains?</h2><p>The remaining household exclusion and cash that could pass without federal estate tax are <b>unknown</b>. Do not subtract only a house value. The estate computation includes includible assets, prior taxable gifts, deductions, credits and any valid portability. Filing threshold and actual liability are different. Crossing a threshold is not itself a tax penalty; late filing/payment and tax liability are separate issues.</p>'''+notice('No fabricated household cash threshold','No estate inventory, prior-gift history, citizenship/residency determination, trust inclusion analysis or portability election has been verified. No local estate-tax threshold is established in this audit; local property, recording and sale charges are separate and parcel/transaction dependent. Current California Controller guidance is not a guarantee about every local charge.')+table('SYNTHETIC future exclusion sensitivity · not actual statutory indexing',['Year','Official future amount','0% assumed growth','2% assumed growth','4% assumed growth','Official starting authority'],future,'illustration')+'''<p>Arithmetic only: published 2027 exclusion × (1 + assumed rate)^(year − 2027). The 0% / 2% / 4% paths are invented, not IRS amounts or replicas of statutory rounding and CPI mechanics. Revisit at transfer; lower-exclusion legislation could reverse apparent headroom. No future estate tax calculation is represented as official.</p>''')

costs=[
('A · primary residence insurance','','UNVERIFIED · official premium-comparison tools are not a binding quote; Form 401 excludes quake, flood, mold and 60+ day vacancy. Check replacement cost, deductible, liability and occupancy.','cdires'),
('A · landlord insurance','','UNVERIFIED · match actual lease use, loss-of-rent and liability cover; do not reuse a homeowners estimate.','insurance'),
('B · mixed owner/rental insurance','','UNVERIFIED · disclose actual occupancy and rentals; no official property-specific quote obtained.','insurance'),
('A and B · water / wastewater','','UNVERIFIED · drinking-water, wastewater and stormwater providers may differ. Identify each from current bills and check its adopted rate schedule, meter and connection charges privately. The linked Water Boards tool only helps identify a drinking-water system; it does not verify a property rate or wastewater provider.','water'),
('A and B · electricity / gas','','UNVERIFIED · electric tariff, grid imports, annual true-up, any fixed charge and rate plan depend on provider, interconnection and enrollment; any gas bill must be confirmed with its provider. No zero bill or solar cash profit assumed. The linked fixed-charge resolution concerns PG&E implementation, not every utility or a property-specific bill.',['cpuc','cpucfixed']),
('A · solar compensation','','UNVERIFIED · bill credits do not prove cash profit; confirm legacy tariff, transfer treatment, system condition and replacement.','cpuc'),
('A and B · maintenance / capital','','UNVERIFIED · inspections and replacement schedules needed; separate routine deductible repairs from capital outlays.','rent'),
('A · assessed value and tax','','UNVERIFIED · no parcel lookup attempted; personal bill history withheld. Reassessment, direct charges and supplementals separate.','boe'),
('B · assessed value and tax','','UNVERIFIED · already owned; A’s inheritance alone is not a change of B’s ownership. Actual title and exceptions unknown.','rtc'),
('Rental income / vacancy / management','','UNVERIFIED · leases and lawful rents, collection, management and turnover costs not confirmed. Existing income cannot be counted as new incremental benefit.','rent'),
('Debt / sale / settlement costs','','UNVERIFIED · loan balances, offers, commissions, recording costs and estate allocations not supplied as official evidence.','basis')]
